  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Comprehensive Protection Programme for Vulnerable Migrant Populations and Host Communities in Morocco</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project&#x2019;s general objective is to contribute to national efforts to reinforce access to comprehensive protection services for migrants and host communities by:1.       Improving access to information on the needs of vulnerable migrants and host communities in Morocco.2. Strengthening the capacity and response capability of institutional and associative actors involved in the protection of vulnerable migrants and targeted vulnerable populations, notably Unaccompanied and Separated Children (UASC) and Victims of trafficking (VoT).3. Enhancing the protection and well-being of migrants in vulnerable situations through the provision of direct assistance, including health care and legal assistance.4.       Supporting local community and migrants in situation of vulnerability with information and means, generating alternatives to irregular migration.5.       Promoting the socio-economic integration of youth in vulnerable situations in Tanger and Tetouan. 6.       Increasing and strengthening preparation, return and reintegration of returnees to reach levels of economic self-sufficiency and social stability within their communities of origin.</narrative>
  </description>
